            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0131" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.0641/87: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at London (Frazer)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-12T18:00:00-05:00">October 12, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 5, 4 p.m. Treasury Department states “It is not the intention of
                    this Department to make any general request of British consular officers for
                    information concerning the compensation paid American citizens prior to the
                    calendar year 1933, regardless of the fact that British tax inspectors are
                    seeking information as to compensation paid British subjects for earlier
                    periods.”</p>
                <p>Endeavor to obtain reciprocal treatment for clerks in consular offices.
                    Retroactive effect was not intended by reciprocal arrangement of June 28, 1933.
                    Mail complete report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
